            }
          ],
          "question": {
            "text": "One main scale division of a vernier caliper is equal to $m$ units. If ${m}^{\\text {th }}$ division of main scale coincides with $(n+1)^{\\text {th }}$ division of vernier scale, the least count of the vernier caliper is:",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "mQNQH",
              "text": "$\\frac{n}{(n+1)}$",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            },
            {
              "id": "nvNHx",
              "text": "$\\frac{\\mathrm{m}}{(\\mathrm{n}+1)}$",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": true
            },
            {
              "id": "yuWWu",
              "text": "$\\frac{1}{(\\mathrm{n}+1)}$",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            },
            {
              "id": "c5gUb",
              "text": "$\\frac{\\mathrm{m}}{\\mathrm{n}(\\mathrm{n}+1)}$",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "Given 1 Main scale division = m\n$\\mathrm{n} M S D=(\\mathrm{n}+1) \\mathrm{VSD}$\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad 1 \\mathrm{VSD}=\\frac{\\mathrm{n}}{\\mathrm{n}+1} \\mathrm{MSD}$\nLeast count of vernier caliper $=1 \\mathrm{MSD}-1 \\mathrm{VSD}$\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad L . C=m-m\\left(\\frac{n}{n+1}\\right)=\\left(1-\\frac{n}{n+1}\\right) m$\n$=m\\left(\\frac{n+1-n}{n+1}\\right)=\\left(\\frac{1}{n+1}\\right) m \\Rightarrow L \\cdot C=\\left(\\frac{m}{n+1}\\right)$",
            "image": null
          },
