            "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/OqbZXdYbXXHnqfLVcxwLEePOLZcLRysHouszNpdF9gU.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\n\r\nAt null point $\\frac{R_{1}}{R_{2}}=\\frac{R_{3}}{R_{4}}=\\frac{x}{100-x}$\r\n\r\nIf radius of the wire is doubled, then the resistance of $A C$ will change and also the resistance of $C B$ will change. But since\r\n\r\n$\\frac{R_{1}}{R_{2}}$ does not change so, $\\frac{R_{3}}{R_{4}}$ should also not change at null point. Therefore the point $C$ does not change.",
